        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "The task is complete. I've successfully fitted the G and 2D peaks of the graphene Raman spectrum and written the results to `/app/results.json`.\n\n**Summary of the fitting process:**\n1. Loaded the data from `/app/graphene.dat` (tab-separated with comma decimal separators)\n2. The x-values were in decreasing order and in units of 0.1 cm⁻¹, so I reversed and converted to cm⁻¹\n3. **G peak** (1520-1650 cm⁻¹ region): Fitted with a Lorentzian + linear background\n   - x₀ = 1619.32 cm⁻¹\n   - γ = 23.25 cm⁻¹\n   - Amplitude = 2384.19\n   - Offset (background at peak center) = 15786.95\n4. **2D peak** (2500-2900 cm⁻¹ region): Fitted by first subtracting linear background, then fitting Lorentzian with fixed gamma (tested 25, 30, 35 cm⁻¹; γ=25 gave best RMS)\n   - x₀ = 2652.46 cm⁻¹\n   - γ = 25.00 cm⁻¹ (fixed)\n   - Amplitude = 241.24\n   - Offset (background at peak center) = 15986.05\n\nThe results.json file has the exact format requested.",
